From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:18:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] airconv, d3d12: 64-bit atomics on buffers and groupshared
 memory

Metal has 64-bit atomics only as unsigned min/max without a result, on device
memory; those map to it directly. Add, and, or and xor are split into two
32-bit atomics (add carries into the high half). Everything else (exchange,
compare-exchange, signed min/max, results of min/max) takes a lock word: a
4096-word table per D3D12 device, passed as one more root argument qword after
the parameters (and the heap addresses), or 32 threadgroup words for
groupshared memory, zeroed before the shader body. Once a shader needs the lock
in an address space, all its 64-bit atomics there use it. Every lane of a SIMD
group stays in the lock loop until all are done (simd_any), so the lane that
holds the lock always reaches its release.

Also: groupshared cmpxchg instructions (32-bit too), D3D12 OPTIONS9/OPTIONS11,
and airconv -rootsig to convert with the shader's embedded root signature.
